Today’s session focused on designing forms in HTML and applying validation to control user input. The mentor explained how forms are used to collect different types of data from users.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ HTML Forms

The <form> tag is used to create forms in HTML.

It contains input elements to collect user data.

Important attributes:

action → Specifies where to send form data

method → Defines HTTP method (GET/POST)

2️⃣ Form Elements

The mentor introduced various input elements:

<input type="text"> → Text field

<input type="password"> → Password field

<input type="radio"> → Select one option

<input type="checkbox"> → Select multiple options

<select> → Dropdown menu

<textarea> → Multi-line input

3️⃣ Form Validation

Validation ensures that users enter correct and required data.

Common validation attributes:

required → Field must be filled

pattern → Defines input format

type="email" → Valid email format

type="number" → Only numeric input

